WEBVTT

1
00:00:20.073 --> 00:00:21.553
Ben looked down at his notes.

2
00:00:21.573 --> 00:00:24.574
"I have enough quotes about Mr.

3
00:00:24.614 --> 00:00:26.174
Freaky's sculpture," he thought.

4
00:00:26.194 --> 00:00:29.275
"I should probably interview the witches next."

5
00:00:29.835 --> 00:00:31.936
His article was due on Friday morning.

6
00:00:33.452 --> 00:00:36.134
Screech! A loud noise filled the hallway.

7
00:00:36.154 --> 00:00:37.234
"Watch out!"

8
00:00:37.594 --> 00:00:38.395
Ben looked up.

9
00:00:38.715 --> 00:00:40.876
He was pretty sure that was Pixel's voice.

10
00:00:41.697 --> 00:00:42.857
Crash! Boom!

11
00:00:43.638 --> 00:00:45.399
The zombies were now wide awake.

12
00:00:45.419 --> 00:00:48.240
"Wh-what is that thing?"

13
00:00:48.641 --> 00:00:49.881
a fish monster yelled.

14
00:00:49.901 --> 00:00:51.262
"It's Mr.

15
00:00:51.302 --> 00:00:52.523
Freaky's sculpture!"

16
00:00:52.883 --> 00:00:53.743
a blob said.

17
00:00:53.763 --> 00:00:55.624
"And it's alive!"

18
00:00:56.265 --> 00:00:57.345
Ben spun around.

19
00:00:58.106 --> 00:01:01.728
Sure enough, the massive sculpture had stopped spinning in place.

20
00:01:03.864 --> 00:01:06.865
Now it was rolling forward—right toward the crowd!

21
00:01:06.885 --> 00:01:09.406
"Run for your lives!"

22
00:01:09.846 --> 00:01:10.946
a werewolf howled.

23
00:01:11.626 --> 00:01:16.068
Students dived out of the way as the metal monster sputtered and screeched.

24
00:01:16.708 --> 00:01:18.428
Its parts spun and twisted.

25
00:01:21.829 --> 00:01:25.050
Ben shot backward as the sculpture rolled toward him.

26
00:01:26.311 --> 00:01:30.352
It rumbled closer and closer and then moved right through him!

27
00:01:32.116 --> 00:01:36.339
Crash! The sculpture smashed into the bank of lockers behind Ben.

28
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:40.162
Everybody ducked as metal parts flew through the air.

29
00:01:40.182 --> 00:01:43.585
"Phew!" Ben gasped.

30
00:01:43.605 --> 00:01:45.246
"That was a close call!"

31
00:01:46.987 --> 00:01:50.209
Mr. Freaky ran down the hall and dropped to his knees.

32
00:01:50.229 --> 00:01:55.453
"My precious sculpture—it's ruined!"

33
00:01:57.135 --> 00:01:58.836
Ms. Van Ghoul hurried forward.

34
00:02:01.156 --> 00:02:03.378
"I'm sure you can piece it back together, Mr.

35
00:02:03.418 --> 00:02:05.800
Freaky." "But Mr.

36
00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:06.901
Freaky shook his head.

37
00:02:06.921 --> 00:02:11.726
"Isn't Leonardo da Creepy coming tomorrow?"

38
00:02:11.746 --> 00:02:14.248
"Yes," Ms.

39
00:02:14.268 --> 00:02:15.028
Van Ghoul said.

40
00:02:15.048 --> 00:02:19.252
"He wants to make sure that our art is up to his artistic standards.

41
00:02:19.833 --> 00:02:21.314
It's just a quick inspection.

42
00:02:21.714 --> 00:02:24.036
He'll be back on Friday night for the big event."

43
00:02:25.057 --> 00:02:26.919
Mr. Freaky gave a heavy sigh.

44
00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:31.882
"I wanted him to see Moving Inspiration while he was here.

45
00:02:32.763 --> 00:02:34.564
But I guess it can wait."

46
00:02:35.465 --> 00:02:39.047
He picked up a twisted metal pipe and stared at it gloomily.

47
00:02:39.067 --> 00:02:43.791
"My sculpture was working fine this morning," he muttered.

48
00:02:43.811 --> 00:02:48.514
"I think somebody sabotaged it!"

49
00:02:49.615 --> 00:02:53.958
Mr. Freaky started gathering up the broken pieces of Moving Inspiration.

50
00:02:56.259 --> 00:02:57.392
Meanwhile Ms.

51
00:02:57.452 --> 00:03:00.614
Van Ghoul waved some students over to a quiet spot.

52
00:03:01.555 --> 00:03:05.457
Until now, the art teacher hadn't seemed bothered by the vandalism.

53
00:03:05.977 --> 00:03:08.859
This time, however, Ben thought she looked worried.

54
00:03:08.879 --> 00:03:13.781
"Leonardo da Creepy is a famous artist," Ms.

55
00:03:13.821 --> 00:03:17.764
Van Ghoul began, "and he's very, very picky.

56
00:03:18.684 --> 00:03:21.366
We cannot let any other problems happen this week.

57
00:03:22.126 --> 00:03:23.347
Otherwise, Mr.

58
00:03:23.387 --> 00:03:25.128
da Creepy might not participate."

59
00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:27.561
A goblin gasped.

60
00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:30.703
"But he's supposed to give us a new painting!"

61
00:03:30.723 --> 00:03:35.366
"Yeah. It could be another Moaning Lisa," a blob added.

62
00:03:35.386 --> 00:03:39.428
"A painting like that could make Monster Academy famous!"

63
00:03:39.448 --> 00:03:41.069
"I know."

64
00:03:41.489 --> 00:03:43.230
Ms. Van Ghoul nodded in agreement.

65
00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:48.834
"I've spent a lot of time convincing him to come here to celebrate Art Week with us.

66
00:03:50.255 --> 00:03:51.956
It would be awful if he canceled.

67
00:03:53.768 --> 00:03:58.850
So if you know anything about who is causing all the trouble, please tell me immediately."

68
00:04:03.112 --> 00:04:08.274
Ben looked down, wondering if he should say something about the trail of paint drops in the gym.

69
00:04:08.834 --> 00:04:11.596
It was a clue—maybe even a big clue.

70
00:04:12.336 --> 00:04:15.337
But a part of him was still worried that Mog was involved.

71
00:04:15.937 --> 00:04:17.898
Ben didn't want his friend to get in trouble.

72
00:04:17.918 --> 00:04:22.080
"I won't say anything yet," Ben thought.

73
00:04:22.728 --> 00:04:28.630
If he kept interviewing monsters and teachers for his story, he might learn more about what was going

74
00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:31.731
on. Suddenly he had an idea.

75
00:04:32.771 --> 00:04:36.112
Pixel had been taking a ton of photos all week long.

76
00:04:37.473 --> 00:04:39.453
Maybe his camera held some clues.

77
00:04:41.574 --> 00:04:44.135
Ben darted off, looking for Pixel.

78
00:04:45.495 --> 00:04:50.711
As he flew past the art room, he saw Mog and the Doppel Gang in there, helping the

79
00:04:50.771 --> 00:04:52.472
mummies make the pyramids.

80
00:04:53.813 --> 00:04:55.635
Ben felt a wave of relief.

81
00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:57.937
"That's good," he thought.

82
00:04:57.957 --> 00:05:01.220
"It looks like Mog has been too busy to mess with Mr.

83
00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:02.080
Freaky's sculpture."

84
00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:04.562
"Has anyone seen Pixel?"

85
00:05:04.903 --> 00:05:06.404
Ben called into the classroom.

86
00:05:07.285 --> 00:05:08.666
They all shook their heads.

87
00:05:08.686 --> 00:05:11.288
"No." "Thanks."

88
00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:15.692
Ben's next stop was the newspaper office.

89
00:05:17.944 --> 00:05:18.725
"There you are!"

90
00:05:19.105 --> 00:05:19.706
Ben said.

91
00:05:20.426 --> 00:05:24.750
Pixel sat at a desk, staring at his camera with a worried expression.

92
00:05:29.114 --> 00:05:29.874
you okay?"

93
00:05:31.676 --> 00:05:33.597
"No." Pixel shook his head.

94
00:05:33.617 --> 00:05:37.020
"Something happened to my camera.

95
00:05:38.121 --> 00:05:39.603
It went dead as soon as Mr.

96
00:05:39.663 --> 00:05:41.584
Freaky's sculpture stopped moving."

97
00:05:42.145 --> 00:05:42.985
He bit his lip.

98
00:05:43.005 --> 00:05:45.728
"It seems to be working again now.

99
00:05:46.444 --> 00:05:48.806
But most of the photos I took are gone."

100
00:05:48.826 --> 00:05:51.708
"What?" Ben's heart sank.

101
00:05:52.288 --> 00:05:56.431
He needed those photos for his article—not to mention his investigation.

102
00:05:56.451 --> 00:05:59.273
"Don't worry," Pixel said quickly.

103
00:05:59.293 --> 00:06:04.136
"As long as my camera is working, I can take some more photos today and tomorrow.

104
00:06:04.876 --> 00:06:07.438
I'll have plenty for the story and the school website."

105
00:06:07.458 --> 00:06:11.821
"Okay." Ben nodded, hoping Pixel was right.

106
00:06:11.841 --> 00:06:13.062
"Sounds good.

107
00:06:13.542 --> 00:06:16.325
Thanks. In the meantime Mr.

108
00:06:16.365 --> 00:06:18.707
Freaky wants me to find out what happened with his sculpture.

109
00:06:19.268 --> 00:06:22.692
Did you happen to notice anything suspicious while you were taking photos?"

110
00:06:22.712 --> 00:06:25.195
"Nope," Pixel said.

111
00:06:25.215 --> 00:06:27.898
"Sorry, but I didn't see a thing."
